{"seq":26,"ts_us":1793634751957355,"service":"agentd","trace_id":"a2f7dd96f090e9ceba17513ad5fb22a1","payload":{"kind":"ag_ui","type":"TOOL_CALL_ARGS","toolCallId":"call_70f339aeba69420bb86e27d3","delta":"{\"text\":\"What's on right now: the screen and Wi\\u2011Fi (both because your request is in flight), and nothing else \\u2014 Bluetooth is off (rfkill\\u2011blocked), the local model is off, and no services are running in the svcd executor. The idle timeout is 120 seconds and the phone has only been idle 2 seconds, so the plan is a dry run that changes nothing: it would keep the screen, Wi\\u2011Fi and local model as they are while a request is in flight, and just wait on Bluetooth and services, which are already off. Nothing was switched off \\u2014 agentd doesn't execute those commands, it only names what an operator would run.\"}"}}
